==Solution 5 (Desperate)==
Taking a look at the diagram, points <imath>M</imath> and <imath>A</imath> seem to divide <imath>\overline{XY}</imath> and <imath>\overline{YZ}</imath> into <imath>1:3</imath> ratios. With this assumption in mind, <imath>XM=2</imath>, <imath>MY=6</imath>, <imath>YA=3</imath>, and <imath>AZ=1</imath>. This means that the areas of <imath>\triangle WXM</imath> and <imath>\triangle WZA</imath> are <imath>\frac{4(2)}{2}=4</imath> and <imath>\frac{8(1)}{2}=4</imath> respectively, and the area of <imath>\triangle MAY</imath> is <imath>\frac{6(3)}{2}=9</imath>. The area of rectangle <imath>WXYZ=4(8)=32</imath>, so subtracting the areas of triangles <imath>WXM</imath>, <imath>WZA</imath>, and <imath>MAY</imath>, we get that the area of <imath>\triangle WMA=32-4-4-9=\boxed{\textbf{(C) 15}}</imath>

~phinetium (first edit!)

==China Test Solution (Finding <imath>\triangle MAY</imath>)==
From solution 3, instead of finding the area of <imath>\triangle WMA</imath>, we instead find  the area of <imath>\triangle MAY</imath>. Then <imath>x = 1</imath> then we have <imath>MA = 8 - 2x = 6</imath>. Again, since <imath>AY = 4 - x</imath>, then <imath>AY = 4 - 1 = 3.</imath> The area of a triangle with legs <imath>3</imath> and <imath>6</imath> is <imath>\frac{3 * 6}{2} = \boxed{9}</imath>.

~pepper2831 (again)

